1
00:00:35,145 --> 00:00:36,305
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:36,305 --> 00:00:37,255
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,255 --> 00:00:38,345
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:00:39,848 --> 00:00:43,089
Don't go, Yi Jae. Please...

5
00:00:52,616 --> 00:00:54,254
Soo Bin.

6
00:00:56,565 --> 00:00:59,139
I love you...

7
00:01:00,332 --> 00:01:02,693
but you're not my dream.

8
00:01:07,297 --> 00:01:09,277
[Final Episode]

9
00:01:24,439 --> 00:01:28,693
Even if you leave, I won't let go of us.

10
00:01:28,693 --> 00:01:30,029
You know what I mean.

11
00:01:30,029 --> 00:01:32,468
You don't get it.

12
00:01:32,468 --> 00:01:36,122
If I leave, that means letting us go.

13
00:01:36,122 --> 00:01:39,012
It's only two years.

14
00:01:39,012 --> 00:01:40,282
Why do we have to break up?

15
00:01:40,282 --> 00:01:44,209
If I go with you beside me,
I'll lean on you there too.

16
00:01:44,209 --> 00:01:45,766
Then nothing will change.

17
00:01:45,766 --> 00:01:49,743
Look. You just took the chairs from me.

18
00:01:49,743 --> 00:01:51,423
- So what?
- Woo Soo Bin.

19
00:01:51,423 --> 00:01:53,220
Do you really not get it?

20
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:55,846
If I stay with you, you'll only look at me too.

21
00:01:55,846 --> 00:01:59,014
Will you spend your life worrying about me?

22
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,590
This isn't what I pictured for us.

23
00:02:04,590 --> 00:02:06,461
Not for me.

24
00:02:06,461 --> 00:02:07,482
Not for you either.

25
00:02:07,482 --> 00:02:10,929
Why do you keep saying we can't stay like this?

26
00:02:13,722 --> 00:02:15,650
You said you love me.

27
00:02:18,476 --> 00:02:22,875
- You said you cared.
- That's why I'm not going to love you anymore!

28
00:02:30,371 --> 00:02:33,383
Why are you making me say something like this?

29
00:02:35,344 --> 00:02:38,218
I'm sorry. I should go.

30
00:02:59,953 --> 00:03:02,094
[2026 Bunam International
Cinema Residency Application]

31
00:03:02,767 --> 00:03:04,347
[Field: Film]

32
00:03:11,168 --> 00:03:13,583
[Applicant Name: Ju Yi Jae]

33
00:03:26,853 --> 00:03:30,383
<i>Are you leaving me out because of my leg?</i>

34
00:03:30,383 --> 00:03:33,313
<i>How does some no-name college grad
just waltz in?</i>

35
00:03:33,313 --> 00:03:36,078
<i>- Calm down.
- What the...</i>

36
00:03:36,903 --> 00:03:39,449
<i>No. Nobody said anything.</i>

37
00:03:39,449 --> 00:03:41,239
<i>Isn't that weird?</i>

38
00:03:41,239 --> 00:03:44,941
<i>No one asks who I am
or why I'm co-directing this.</i>

39
00:03:44,941 --> 00:03:46,945
<i>Help me, Soo Bin.</i>

40
00:03:48,001 --> 00:03:50,443
<i>Help me keep running.</i>

41
00:04:12,095 --> 00:04:13,538
Hello, sir.

42
00:04:13,538 --> 00:04:16,686
The guitar piece for our reunion scene.

43
00:04:16,686 --> 00:04:19,116
I cleaned up the noise as much as I could,

44
00:04:19,116 --> 00:04:21,411
but I couldn't remove all the set noise.

45
00:04:21,411 --> 00:04:23,671
Come on. That's my job.

46
00:04:23,671 --> 00:04:26,287
Just send me the footage, Director Ju.

47
00:04:26,287 --> 00:04:28,331
<i>Then I'll send it right now.</i>

48
00:04:28,331 --> 00:04:30,673
But while I was organizing it, I had a thought.

49
00:04:30,673 --> 00:04:33,897
If we can't get it clean anyway,

50
00:04:33,897 --> 00:04:35,756
what if we make it sound like a gramophone?

51
00:04:35,756 --> 00:04:37,090
<i>A gramophone?</i>

52
00:04:37,090 --> 00:04:38,091
Yeah.

53
00:04:38,091 --> 00:04:42,046
<i>That would cover the audio quality issue,</i>

54
00:04:42,046 --> 00:04:43,636
<i>and it would add to the period feel.</i>

55
00:04:43,636 --> 00:04:46,642
Please talk it over
with Director Woo and let me know.

56
00:04:46,642 --> 00:04:48,652
Okay... Oh, right.

57
00:04:48,652 --> 00:04:51,835
Is something going on with Director Woo lately?

58
00:04:52,829 --> 00:04:55,108
I don't know. Why?

59
00:04:55,108 --> 00:04:57,482
<i>He just seems...</i>

60
00:04:58,318 --> 00:04:59,514
<i>Never mind.</i>

61
00:04:59,514 --> 00:05:02,282
<i>I'll call you later. Have a good one.</i>

62
00:05:02,282 --> 00:05:03,882
Yeah.

63
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,476
Alright.

64
00:05:28,476 --> 00:05:31,924
<i>♪ Shall we... ♪</i>

65
00:05:31,924 --> 00:05:32,967
Wait...

66
00:05:32,967 --> 00:05:35,148
Oh my gosh!

67
00:05:35,148 --> 00:05:36,575
Hey!

68
00:05:36,575 --> 00:05:39,220
You scared me!

69
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:41,445
I thought about it...

70
00:05:41,445 --> 00:05:42,697
What?

71
00:05:42,697 --> 00:05:44,205
Are you sleep-talking?

72
00:05:44,205 --> 00:05:46,285
Why are you sleeping here?

73
00:05:46,285 --> 00:05:47,961
Go home already.

74
00:05:47,961 --> 00:05:51,623
Listen. That guitar piece we were going to use.

75
00:05:51,623 --> 00:05:54,245
If we can't isolate it cleanly,

76
00:05:54,245 --> 00:05:58,308
why not make it sound like a gramophone?

77
00:05:58,308 --> 00:06:00,886
Like it's from the street.

78
00:06:02,141 --> 00:06:05,238
Did you just talk to Director Ju?

79
00:06:05,238 --> 00:06:06,455
What?

80
00:06:06,455 --> 00:06:09,748
You said the exact same thing she did.

81
00:06:09,748 --> 00:06:13,633
I came here to work on that.

82
00:06:15,101 --> 00:06:17,104
By the way...

83
00:06:17,104 --> 00:06:20,693
Who's Sim Shin?

84
00:06:20,693 --> 00:06:24,823
Where did you find the hidden master?

85
00:06:24,823 --> 00:06:27,283
Back up a little.

86
00:06:27,283 --> 00:06:32,247
He's actor Sim Yu Geon's father.

87
00:06:32,247 --> 00:06:34,184
Awesome! Seriously?

88
00:06:34,184 --> 00:06:36,878
His playing was something else.

89
00:06:36,878 --> 00:06:41,585
No flashy technique, but it hits you hard.

90
00:06:41,585 --> 00:06:42,716
This is exciting.

91
00:06:42,716 --> 00:06:44,615
Hold on...

92
00:06:44,615 --> 00:06:46,386
Alright.

93
00:06:50,697 --> 00:06:52,341
Time to work. Please leave.

94
00:06:52,341 --> 00:06:53,352
Yeah.

95
00:06:53,352 --> 00:06:56,394
Go ahead. Do your exciting work.

96
00:06:56,394 --> 00:06:58,951
If you're staying here, pay some rent.

97
00:06:58,951 --> 00:07:02,230
If I don't push you, you always miss deadlines.

98
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:04,468
- Just turn on the computer.
- Wait.

99
00:07:04,468 --> 00:07:08,328
How about this when Moo Gyeom gets chased?

100
00:07:12,130 --> 00:07:14,080
Are we in Africa?

101
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:16,916
This is Gyeongseong.

102
00:07:16,916 --> 00:07:20,221
You really know nothing about music.

103
00:07:23,826 --> 00:07:25,552
[Final Results for
the Bunam International Cinema Residency]

104
00:07:25,552 --> 00:07:27,336
[You have been selected for
the Bunam International Cinema Residency]

105
00:07:27,336 --> 00:07:29,345
[Congratulations, Director Ju Yi Jae]

106
00:07:46,946 --> 00:07:50,325
[Dream, Written by Woo Soo Bin]

107
00:07:56,143 --> 00:07:57,983
Woo Soo Bin.

108
00:08:28,424 --> 00:08:30,216
Can I come in?

109
00:08:31,050 --> 00:08:33,133
Sure, come in.

110
00:08:36,412 --> 00:08:39,554
Sorry. That wasn't mine to say.

111
00:08:39,554 --> 00:08:42,415
You got in, didn't you?

112
00:08:42,415 --> 00:08:44,796
You came to tell me, right?

113
00:08:44,796 --> 00:08:46,196
Yeah.

114
00:08:48,650 --> 00:08:50,228
Yi Jae.

115
00:08:51,219 --> 00:08:53,445
Why do you look like that?

116
00:08:54,505 --> 00:08:56,157
I'm sorry.

117
00:09:01,904 --> 00:09:03,459
Look at me.

118
00:09:05,877 --> 00:09:08,022
I was wrong.

119
00:09:10,003 --> 00:09:13,661
I came this far because I loved you.

120
00:09:14,290 --> 00:09:17,758
But then I used that love to ask you to stay.

121
00:09:17,758 --> 00:09:19,849
I was so ashamed.

122
00:09:20,724 --> 00:09:25,493
I forgot my promise to give your dream back.

123
00:09:26,264 --> 00:09:28,388
I'm sorry.

124
00:09:28,388 --> 00:09:31,945
You already did.

125
00:09:31,945 --> 00:09:34,805
Thanks to you, I found my dream again.

126
00:09:34,805 --> 00:09:39,452
For the next two years,
I'll make it bigger and better.

127
00:09:46,257 --> 00:09:48,740
I know you will.

128
00:09:49,723 --> 00:09:52,644
You already shine this bright.

129
00:10:05,544 --> 00:10:08,038
Goodbye, Director Ju Yi Jae.

130
00:10:08,698 --> 00:10:12,631
Wherever you are, whatever you do,
I'll always root for you.

131
00:10:13,897 --> 00:10:15,602
Thank you.

132
00:10:18,097 --> 00:10:20,006
Take care.

133
00:11:00,138 --> 00:11:02,202
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

134
00:11:02,202 --> 00:11:04,722
<i>Finally done!</i>

135
00:11:10,514 --> 00:11:11,644
<i>Cut!</i>

136
00:11:11,644 --> 00:11:13,467
<i>- Okay!
- Okay!</i>

137
00:11:35,856 --> 00:11:37,564
Ju Yi Jae!

138
00:11:51,757 --> 00:11:55,584
Take this with you.

139
00:11:56,651 --> 00:11:59,472
I hope this doesn't keep you from moving on,

140
00:11:59,472 --> 00:12:01,779
but gives you...

141
00:12:02,827 --> 00:12:05,017
the strength to endure.

142
00:12:05,633 --> 00:12:08,607
Like "Gyeongseong Love Song" did for me.

143
00:12:53,968 --> 00:12:55,991
Did you tell your dad?

144
00:12:55,991 --> 00:12:58,698
That his playing will be in our film?

145
00:12:58,698 --> 00:12:59,795
Yes.

146
00:12:59,795 --> 00:13:02,598
He was thrilled.

147
00:13:02,598 --> 00:13:06,222
He watches your video
in his hospital room every day.

148
00:13:06,222 --> 00:13:08,468
I'm glad he likes it.

149
00:13:15,222 --> 00:13:16,733
Yi Jae.

150
00:13:16,733 --> 00:13:19,563
You know I'm your biggest fan, right?

151
00:13:19,563 --> 00:13:21,157
Of course I do.

152
00:13:21,157 --> 00:13:24,581
If I hadn't had you in Seoul,
where I knew no one,

153
00:13:24,581 --> 00:13:27,923
I couldn't have held on.

154
00:13:27,923 --> 00:13:32,380
The chicken you brought,
saying you couldn't finish it alone.

155
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:36,534
The calls for no real reason.

156
00:13:36,534 --> 00:13:39,200
I knew it was all you cheering me on.

157
00:13:43,065 --> 00:13:45,216
So...

158
00:13:45,216 --> 00:13:49,598
If it gets lonely or hard there,
you have to tell me.

159
00:13:49,598 --> 00:13:50,688
Hey.

160
00:13:50,688 --> 00:13:51,728
I'm Ju Yi Jae.

161
00:13:51,728 --> 00:13:54,098
That's why I'm saying it.

162
00:13:54,098 --> 00:13:58,988
Don't suffer alone
just because you hate looking weak.

163
00:14:00,832 --> 00:14:03,479
So cheesy.

164
00:14:03,479 --> 00:14:05,505
Just have your soup.

165
00:14:14,576 --> 00:14:16,700
- Hey, Ju Young Jae!
- What?

166
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:20,810
Just quit already!

167
00:14:20,810 --> 00:14:23,420
What is it now?

168
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:25,747
Did you even taste it before serving it?

169
00:14:25,747 --> 00:14:27,151
Try this!

170
00:14:27,151 --> 00:14:30,458
Look at the great food critic.

171
00:14:36,631 --> 00:14:38,537
Darn it! Water!

172
00:14:38,537 --> 00:14:40,912
Water! Water!

173
00:14:44,613 --> 00:14:46,463
I'll add more water.

174
00:14:46,463 --> 00:14:48,518
Sorry.

175
00:14:50,430 --> 00:14:52,166
I'll apologize for him.

176
00:14:53,330 --> 00:14:57,198
You said you'd be there two years.
Why pack only winter clothes?

177
00:14:57,198 --> 00:15:01,456
I looked it up.
Mon-tree-all has all four seasons too.

178
00:15:01,456 --> 00:15:03,821
It's Montreal, idiot.

179
00:15:03,821 --> 00:15:06,387
Let her be. She can buy things there.

180
00:15:06,387 --> 00:15:09,220
Since when do you tell anyone to buy things?

181
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:12,291
Mom. I can't take all this anyway.

182
00:15:12,291 --> 00:15:13,597
Why not?

183
00:15:13,597 --> 00:15:16,033
You're not carrying it. The plane is.

184
00:15:16,033 --> 00:15:19,892
I heard there are lots of
Korean restaurants there.

185
00:15:25,067 --> 00:15:27,357
Then take this.

186
00:15:27,357 --> 00:15:28,944
What is it?

187
00:15:28,944 --> 00:15:31,788
- Money?
- Give it back. That's for your sister.

188
00:15:31,788 --> 00:15:34,881
This has to be at least a million won!

189
00:15:36,871 --> 00:15:38,195
Come on.

190
00:15:38,195 --> 00:15:40,048
What money do you have?

191
00:15:40,048 --> 00:15:42,429
Just pay off your loan interest.

192
00:15:42,429 --> 00:15:44,125
Keep it as emergency cash.

193
00:15:44,125 --> 00:15:46,505
Don't scrape by over there.

194
00:15:46,505 --> 00:15:48,362
I said I'm fine.

195
00:15:48,362 --> 00:15:51,530
It's not like I'm leaving forever.
I'll be back soon.

196
00:15:51,530 --> 00:15:54,433
She's right. Two years will fly by.

197
00:15:54,433 --> 00:15:56,759
Just think of it as sending her to the army.

198
00:15:56,759 --> 00:15:59,056
When I got discharged, you said, "Already?"

199
00:15:59,056 --> 00:16:00,983
That's not the same!

200
00:16:00,983 --> 00:16:03,540
Why are you yelling at me again?

201
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:05,564
You silly girl!

202
00:16:05,564 --> 00:16:08,397
When your mom gives you something,
just take it!

203
00:16:08,397 --> 00:16:12,173
It breaks my heart
that I never did enough for you.

204
00:16:12,173 --> 00:16:13,945
Okay.

205
00:16:13,945 --> 00:16:16,098
I'll take them.

206
00:16:19,518 --> 00:16:21,215
What do you want to eat?

207
00:16:21,215 --> 00:16:23,380
Let's just have dinner.

208
00:16:23,380 --> 00:16:25,125
Kimchi fried rice.

209
00:16:25,125 --> 00:16:26,714
Fine.

210
00:16:27,375 --> 00:16:30,219
Ju Young Jae! Come cut the kimchi!

211
00:16:30,219 --> 00:16:32,965
I've been chopping things all day.

212
00:16:32,965 --> 00:16:34,687
Move. Now.

213
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:42,163
Chop it nice.

214
00:16:42,163 --> 00:16:43,946
Yes, ma'am.

215
00:16:56,578 --> 00:17:01,471
I never dreamed that
to hold one man in my arms,

216
00:17:01,471 --> 00:17:07,099
<i>I'd risk my life, take up a gun,
and cross a border.</i>

217
00:17:08,790 --> 00:17:11,660
<i>What an extraordinary man you are.</i>

218
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:15,557
<i>So fearless.</i>

219
00:17:15,557 --> 00:17:19,033
<i>What an extraordinary woman you are.</i>

220
00:17:19,033 --> 00:17:21,299
<i>What are you waiting for?</i>

221
00:17:21,299 --> 00:17:23,298
<i>Hold me.</i>

222
00:18:01,727 --> 00:18:04,954
[Directed and Written by
Woo Soo Bin, Ju Yi Jae]

223
00:18:26,963 --> 00:18:29,114
- Good work.
- Thanks.

224
00:18:29,114 --> 00:18:30,484
It's a fine film.

225
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:32,252
Thank you.

226
00:18:32,252 --> 00:18:36,686
At this rate, a release this year
should be no problem.

227
00:18:36,686 --> 00:18:37,700
Yeah.

228
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:39,725
Good work, Director Woo.

229
00:18:39,725 --> 00:18:42,033
Thank you for your hard work.

230
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:44,998
- Thank you.
- Then let's continue this somewhere else.

231
00:18:44,998 --> 00:18:47,441
Yes. Please join us for dinner.

232
00:18:47,441 --> 00:18:49,243
I have a place reserved.

233
00:18:49,243 --> 00:18:50,703
Shall we?

234
00:18:50,703 --> 00:18:52,296
Let's go.

235
00:19:12,442 --> 00:19:13,894
Ian.

236
00:19:16,078 --> 00:19:19,078
I shouldn't say this as your CEO.

237
00:19:19,078 --> 00:19:23,158
But as your brother,
I always choose to go instead of stop.

238
00:19:23,158 --> 00:19:26,419
It's not too late. Go see Yi Jae.

239
00:19:27,764 --> 00:19:30,016
I said go.

240
00:19:32,525 --> 00:19:33,946
Yeah.

241
00:19:34,671 --> 00:19:36,349
Ian!

242
00:19:36,349 --> 00:19:37,512
How are you getting there?

243
00:19:37,512 --> 00:19:39,785
Are you running all the way to the airport?

244
00:19:39,785 --> 00:19:42,578
Here. Take the keys!

245
00:19:53,256 --> 00:19:55,239
[Applicant Recommendation Letter]

246
00:19:55,239 --> 00:19:58,798
<i>I love the world Director Ju Yi Jae creates.</i>

247
00:19:59,639 --> 00:20:04,064
<i>Even in a world overrun with zombies,
she finds warmth.</i>

248
00:20:04,064 --> 00:20:06,713
<i>Even in an age filled with despair,</i>

249
00:20:06,713 --> 00:20:10,609
<i>she still finds hope.</i>

250
00:20:23,827 --> 00:20:28,379
<i>She has a vision that is entirely her own.</i>

251
00:20:29,068 --> 00:20:33,265
<i>And it was a true honor</i>

252
00:20:33,265 --> 00:20:36,080
<i>to be part of Director Ju Yi Jae's world.</i>

253
00:20:37,556 --> 00:20:39,464
[Incheon International Airport]

254
00:20:41,932 --> 00:20:46,250
<i>I still want to remain in that world.</i>

255
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:50,588
<i>And it's still hard to let her go.</i>

256
00:20:54,648 --> 00:20:56,305
- Thank you.
<i>- But I know</i>

257
00:20:56,305 --> 00:20:59,284
<i>she will do great things
in a much bigger world.</i>

258
00:20:59,284 --> 00:21:03,571
<i>So I give her my full support
on the road ahead.</i>

259
00:22:43,552 --> 00:22:46,363
<i>Without a doubt,</i>

260
00:22:47,333 --> 00:22:51,257
<i>Director Ju Yi Jae was
the best partner I have ever had.</i>

261
00:23:20,754 --> 00:23:24,718
[I can do this!]
[Greatness is seeing it through!]

262
00:24:15,575 --> 00:24:17,533
Come on, come on!

263
00:24:40,292 --> 00:24:43,547
[Thursday, December 3, 2026
Final Draft Complete]

264
00:24:49,009 --> 00:24:52,274
[Gyeongseong Love Song Screening, 8 PM]

265
00:25:00,020 --> 00:25:03,095
[Gyeongseong Love Song VIP Screening]

266
00:25:03,095 --> 00:25:06,562
Thank you so much for coming
to the VIP screening.

267
00:25:06,562 --> 00:25:10,330
Now, please welcome
our directors and cast to the stage.

268
00:25:10,330 --> 00:25:13,702
A big round of applause, please.

269
00:25:13,702 --> 00:25:17,104
Looking good, Woo Soo Bin!

270
00:25:17,104 --> 00:25:19,542
You're amazing!

271
00:25:24,963 --> 00:25:26,131
Hello.

272
00:25:26,131 --> 00:25:29,318
I'm Woo Soo Bin,
director of "Gyeongseong Love Song."

273
00:25:29,318 --> 00:25:34,053
Our co-director, Ju Yi Jae,
unfortunately couldn't be with us today.

274
00:25:34,053 --> 00:25:36,677
Thank you for your understanding.

275
00:25:36,677 --> 00:25:41,103
Since you all took the time to be here,
I hope you laugh and cry all you want.

276
00:25:41,103 --> 00:25:42,140
And now...

277
00:25:42,140 --> 00:25:44,444
From action to romance,

278
00:25:44,444 --> 00:25:49,098
please welcome actress Oh Ha Na,
who shines in every genre.

279
00:25:49,098 --> 00:25:51,540
You're gorgeous, Oh Ha Na!

280
00:25:52,298 --> 00:25:57,286
Hello. I'm Oh Ha Na,
aiming to become the queen of romance

281
00:25:57,286 --> 00:25:59,414
with my big-screen debut.

282
00:26:00,706 --> 00:26:01,860
Hello.

283
00:26:01,860 --> 00:26:07,367
I'm rookie actor Sim Yu Geon,
playing Moo Gyeom.

284
00:26:07,367 --> 00:26:10,108
I hope you enjoy my performance. Thank you.

285
00:26:12,336 --> 00:26:16,098
We'll say one final goodbye before we go.

286
00:26:16,098 --> 00:26:18,265
One, two, three.

287
00:26:22,788 --> 00:26:26,986
Amazing. I wonder who they take after.

288
00:26:26,986 --> 00:26:29,542
Maybe I got lucky with my kids.

289
00:26:29,542 --> 00:26:31,858
Which one do you mean?

290
00:26:31,858 --> 00:26:34,835
- Oh my...
- Both, of course!

291
00:26:34,835 --> 00:26:36,910
Who invited you?

292
00:26:36,910 --> 00:26:39,293
- It's a good day, so I came.
- Don't touch me!

293
00:26:39,293 --> 00:26:40,990
- Get away.
- Just a second.

294
00:26:40,990 --> 00:26:42,285
Ma'am.

295
00:26:42,285 --> 00:26:46,557
Your son and daughter turned out great,
just like you.

296
00:26:46,557 --> 00:26:48,029
You...

297
00:26:48,029 --> 00:26:50,426
Oh, did you change salons?

298
00:26:50,426 --> 00:26:51,508
Seriously...

299
00:26:51,508 --> 00:26:53,468
I'll let it slide today.

300
00:26:53,468 --> 00:26:56,671
If Director Ju were here today,

301
00:26:56,671 --> 00:26:59,730
she would've owned this stage.

302
00:26:59,730 --> 00:27:00,905
It's too bad.

303
00:27:00,905 --> 00:27:02,172
True.

304
00:27:02,172 --> 00:27:05,226
Director Ju had one amazing voice.

305
00:27:05,226 --> 00:27:06,438
Gosh...

306
00:27:06,438 --> 00:27:11,835
Feels like yesterday
she marched us all into CEO An's company.

307
00:27:11,835 --> 00:27:14,183
That was already a year ago.

308
00:27:15,159 --> 00:27:17,294
I wonder if she's doing okay.

309
00:27:19,583 --> 00:27:21,345
It's starting.

310
00:27:26,142 --> 00:27:27,712
<i>Yi Jae.</i>

311
00:27:27,712 --> 00:27:30,162
<i>The screening went well.</i>

312
00:27:30,882 --> 00:27:33,647
<i>The after-party was chaos.</i>

313
00:27:34,343 --> 00:27:38,345
<i>The Assistant Director went hard again tonight.</i>

314
00:27:41,361 --> 00:27:45,976
There's still one thing I regret.

315
00:27:45,976 --> 00:27:51,024
I never should've treated Director Ju that way.

316
00:27:51,024 --> 00:27:55,739
You've told me that over ten times.

317
00:27:56,893 --> 00:27:59,233
Did I?

318
00:28:01,113 --> 00:28:02,954
Anyway...

319
00:28:02,954 --> 00:28:05,439
She may be younger than me,

320
00:28:05,439 --> 00:28:09,057
I think she's amazing.

321
00:28:09,057 --> 00:28:11,463
She already made her directorial debut,

322
00:28:11,463 --> 00:28:14,967
but still went abroad to learn more.

323
00:28:14,967 --> 00:28:17,757
That takes real courage.

324
00:28:17,757 --> 00:28:21,846
I could never do that. Never.

325
00:28:21,846 --> 00:28:23,179
You said that too.

326
00:28:23,179 --> 00:28:24,997
Right.

327
00:28:24,997 --> 00:28:26,862
I did.

328
00:28:26,862 --> 00:28:28,747
Then...

329
00:28:28,747 --> 00:28:32,370
Should we save the rest for round three?

330
00:28:32,370 --> 00:28:35,904
Round one was official.
Round two was out of courtesy.

331
00:28:35,904 --> 00:28:38,318
I've done my duty for the night.

332
00:28:38,318 --> 00:28:40,951
Come on!

333
00:28:40,951 --> 00:28:43,493
Round three is for romance.

334
00:28:43,493 --> 00:28:45,605
Round four is for loyalty.

335
00:28:45,605 --> 00:28:47,554
No.

336
00:28:48,577 --> 00:28:50,927
Let's call it a night.

337
00:28:50,927 --> 00:28:54,885
I miss loyal Director Ju.

338
00:28:54,885 --> 00:28:58,957
What time is it in Canada now?

339
00:29:00,923 --> 00:29:02,661
Director Ju.

340
00:29:02,661 --> 00:29:05,343
Director Ju...

341
00:29:07,728 --> 00:29:10,065
[Director Ju]

342
00:29:20,856 --> 00:29:22,548
<i>Hello?</i>

343
00:29:24,492 --> 00:29:26,353
<i>Hello?</i>

344
00:29:26,353 --> 00:29:28,262
<i>Assistant Director?</i>

345
00:29:31,433 --> 00:29:34,202
<i>Are you calling about today's screening?</i>

346
00:29:34,202 --> 00:29:36,092
<i>How did it go?</i>

347
00:29:39,036 --> 00:29:40,496
<i>Huh?</i>

348
00:29:44,867 --> 00:29:47,147
<i>Are you there?</i>

349
00:29:48,964 --> 00:29:51,279
<i>What is this...</i>

350
00:29:52,273 --> 00:29:55,533
<i>This call is expensive. I'm hanging up!</i>

351
00:30:00,745 --> 00:30:02,576
<i>Do you know?</i>

352
00:30:04,532 --> 00:30:07,301
<i>For 24 seconds,</i>

353
00:30:08,203 --> 00:30:10,417
<i>we were together.</i>

354
00:30:42,909 --> 00:30:44,601
What are you listening to?

355
00:30:47,441 --> 00:30:50,052
My dad playing the guitar.

356
00:30:50,052 --> 00:30:51,838
Oh, really?

357
00:31:05,051 --> 00:31:07,749
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

358
00:31:15,816 --> 00:31:17,640
You can lean on me.

359
00:31:34,583 --> 00:31:36,338
<i>Yu Geon.</i>

360
00:31:37,406 --> 00:31:40,459
<i>When should we open our canned pineapple?</i>

361
00:31:42,114 --> 00:31:43,847
<i>In ten thousand years?</i>

362
00:31:48,805 --> 00:31:53,323
<i>Our two leads get their perfect happy ending.</i>

363
00:31:55,227 --> 00:31:58,023
[On-screen lovers become real...
Oh Ha Na and Sim Yu Geon spotted dating]

364
00:31:59,195 --> 00:32:02,449
<i>Maybe. Maybe not.</i>

365
00:32:02,449 --> 00:32:04,131
No way.

366
00:32:05,006 --> 00:32:07,305
Sim Yu Geon!

367
00:32:21,628 --> 00:32:23,144
[Search All: Choi Sa Rang]

368
00:32:24,335 --> 00:32:25,355
Choi Sa Rang?

369
00:32:25,355 --> 00:32:27,475
[Choi Sa Rang]

370
00:32:27,475 --> 00:32:30,073
[Essay: Easy Love, Hard Love]

371
00:32:34,871 --> 00:32:35,905
[Choi Sa Rang]

372
00:32:35,905 --> 00:32:38,014
[Book Search]

373
00:32:38,979 --> 00:32:40,649
Done.

374
00:32:41,731 --> 00:32:46,450
[Choi Sa Rang]

375
00:32:47,246 --> 00:32:48,585
Done.

376
00:32:48,585 --> 00:32:50,501
Now that's how you market.

377
00:32:50,501 --> 00:32:52,618
I'm a genius.

378
00:32:52,618 --> 00:32:54,355
[Trending New Books]

379
00:32:59,630 --> 00:33:01,351
Where did they all go?

380
00:33:01,351 --> 00:33:03,370
What...

381
00:33:03,370 --> 00:33:04,781
Wait.

382
00:33:04,781 --> 00:33:08,719
Excuse me. All my books are gone.

383
00:33:08,719 --> 00:33:11,472
"Easy Love, Hard Love."

384
00:33:11,472 --> 00:33:14,619
That gentleman over there...

385
00:33:21,106 --> 00:33:22,968
In Uk?

386
00:33:27,987 --> 00:33:29,600
Oh, no.

387
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:31,486
You caught me.

388
00:33:42,012 --> 00:33:47,524
<i>As for the people we know,
their ending seems to be open.</i>

389
00:33:49,410 --> 00:33:53,434
This is something I'm personally curious about.

390
00:33:53,434 --> 00:33:59,196
In this film, you're credited
under your real name, Woo Soo Bin.

391
00:33:59,196 --> 00:34:01,863
Is there a special reason?

392
00:34:01,863 --> 00:34:06,513
Since I came back to Korea,
I wanted to be called by my own name.

393
00:34:07,159 --> 00:34:12,247
Every step I've taken was
toward getting that name back.

394
00:34:13,339 --> 00:34:15,203
And finally...

395
00:34:16,576 --> 00:34:18,278
I'm here.

396
00:34:24,379 --> 00:34:26,223
<i>Yi Jae.</i>

397
00:34:26,223 --> 00:34:30,620
<i>I hope this isn't where my story ends.</i>

398
00:35:18,644 --> 00:35:20,670
<i>I miss you.</i>

399
00:35:20,670 --> 00:35:22,324
<i>Yi Jae.</i>

400
00:35:31,292 --> 00:35:33,245
<i>I guess...</i>

401
00:35:35,649 --> 00:35:38,093
<i>I still haven't gotten over you.</i>

402
00:35:41,542 --> 00:35:46,441
<i>I guess I still don't want to wake up
from this dream.</i>

403
00:36:07,103 --> 00:36:08,357
[One year later]

404
00:36:08,357 --> 00:36:10,373
Woo Soo Bin!

405
00:36:14,570 --> 00:36:16,501
Woo Soo Bin!

406
00:36:17,963 --> 00:36:22,420
What happened to this place?
It's a total pigsty.

407
00:36:22,420 --> 00:36:25,239
Why do you always leave your socks unmatched?

408
00:36:25,239 --> 00:36:27,900
What are you even doing?

409
00:36:27,900 --> 00:36:30,420
The festival crew is coming.

410
00:36:30,420 --> 00:36:32,018
I said I'm not doing it.

411
00:36:32,018 --> 00:36:34,841
Just give them a quick greeting.

412
00:36:34,841 --> 00:36:36,718
No.

413
00:36:36,718 --> 00:36:40,270
- What?
- I said no.

414
00:36:40,270 --> 00:36:42,475
You don't want to?

415
00:36:42,475 --> 00:36:44,639
Then write a script.

416
00:36:44,639 --> 00:36:46,158
Nice try.

417
00:36:46,158 --> 00:36:47,715
Stop nagging me.

418
00:36:47,715 --> 00:36:49,635
I'm not joking.

419
00:36:49,635 --> 00:36:52,693
How long will you keep moping around?

420
00:36:52,693 --> 00:36:54,875
You need to work so I can make money too.

421
00:36:54,875 --> 00:36:58,209
You keep turning down every script.

422
00:36:58,209 --> 00:37:00,026
Come on.

423
00:37:00,026 --> 00:37:02,077
You have Director Park and Director Kim.

424
00:37:02,077 --> 00:37:03,966
Tell them to work hard.

425
00:37:03,966 --> 00:37:07,624
They're working hard looking for scripts.

426
00:37:07,624 --> 00:37:11,126
But you already have one.

427
00:37:11,126 --> 00:37:12,910
What script do I have?

428
00:37:12,910 --> 00:37:15,299
"Dream." The one you wrote in the States.

429
00:37:15,299 --> 00:37:18,147
- Oh...
- You remember?

430
00:37:18,147 --> 00:37:20,679
Let's make it. I like that story.

431
00:37:20,679 --> 00:37:23,170
- I don't have it.
- What?

432
00:37:23,170 --> 00:37:25,508
- Yi Jae has it.
- What?

433
00:37:25,508 --> 00:37:27,467
Did you at least scan it?

434
00:37:35,360 --> 00:37:36,653
Let's break up.

435
00:37:36,653 --> 00:37:37,988
We really should.

436
00:37:37,988 --> 00:37:42,238
I'm so sick of this.
Let's say goodbye for real.

437
00:37:42,238 --> 00:37:45,223
I'm already saying goodbye every day.

438
00:37:48,648 --> 00:37:49,813
Hey.

439
00:37:49,813 --> 00:37:53,973
Yi Jae would hate seeing you like this.

440
00:37:54,662 --> 00:37:56,472
This year's Geumseong Film Festival...

441
00:37:56,472 --> 00:37:58,762
Sim Yu Geon and Oh Ha Na are hosting.

442
00:37:58,762 --> 00:38:02,462
They both won Best Newcomer last year,

443
00:38:02,462 --> 00:38:06,558
so there's a special screening
of "Gyeongseong Love Song."

444
00:38:06,558 --> 00:38:07,742
Soo Bin.

445
00:38:07,742 --> 00:38:11,527
I know what "Gyeongseong Love Song"
means to you.

446
00:38:11,527 --> 00:38:16,568
Use this chance to say a proper final goodbye,

447
00:38:16,568 --> 00:38:18,700
and let it go now.

448
00:38:21,898 --> 00:38:23,377
In Uk.

449
00:38:24,738 --> 00:38:28,025
Even you can't stand looking at me?

450
00:38:28,664 --> 00:38:30,404
Am I that pathetic?

451
00:38:33,524 --> 00:38:35,010
Yeah.

452
00:38:36,016 --> 00:38:38,748
I think I'm pathetic too.

453
00:38:38,748 --> 00:38:42,554
Yi Jae will shine even without me.

454
00:38:43,255 --> 00:38:45,418
I'm hopeless.

455
00:38:48,623 --> 00:38:50,249
I'll do it.

456
00:38:55,000 --> 00:38:56,770
Director Woo!

457
00:38:56,770 --> 00:38:58,801
- It's been so long.
- Hello.

458
00:38:58,801 --> 00:39:00,531
- How have you been?
- Please come in.

459
00:39:00,531 --> 00:39:02,017
They're here.

460
00:39:02,017 --> 00:39:04,502
- Hello.
- You made it.

461
00:39:08,191 --> 00:39:09,815
Director Woo?

462
00:39:09,815 --> 00:39:12,836
- It's been so long.
- Right.

463
00:39:12,836 --> 00:39:14,263
You've met before, right?

464
00:39:14,263 --> 00:39:16,668
- He's in charge of today's festival shoot.
- I see.

465
00:39:16,668 --> 00:39:18,794
Director Woo, don't you remember me?

466
00:39:18,794 --> 00:39:22,188
Does it look like I forgot?

467
00:39:23,421 --> 00:39:26,218
You've gotten even pricklier.

468
00:39:26,218 --> 00:39:27,718
Anyway...

469
00:39:28,328 --> 00:39:32,125
I left the network
and started a small production company.

470
00:39:32,824 --> 00:39:34,520
So...

471
00:39:34,520 --> 00:39:37,414
Looking forward to working with you today.

472
00:39:37,414 --> 00:39:39,354
Let's see.

473
00:39:39,354 --> 00:39:41,442
Where should we film?

474
00:39:41,442 --> 00:39:44,047
The view is incredible.

475
00:39:44,047 --> 00:39:46,575
The balcony might be too cold.

476
00:39:46,575 --> 00:39:48,243
This spot looks good.

477
00:39:48,243 --> 00:39:51,049
Yes, let's shoot here.

478
00:39:51,747 --> 00:39:53,370
Would you like some coffee?

479
00:39:53,370 --> 00:39:57,157
Yes, please! Iced Americano, decaf.

480
00:40:03,648 --> 00:40:04,912
Do you have a script?

481
00:40:04,912 --> 00:40:05,952
No.

482
00:40:05,952 --> 00:40:08,062
This plays before the screening, right?

483
00:40:08,062 --> 00:40:09,285
How long do you need?

484
00:40:09,285 --> 00:40:10,289
Well...

485
00:40:10,289 --> 00:40:12,319
About a minute is fine.

486
00:40:12,319 --> 00:40:13,893
Oh, right.

487
00:40:14,559 --> 00:40:18,116
Where's Ju Yi Jae? I don't see her.

488
00:40:18,116 --> 00:40:19,972
Jeez.

489
00:40:20,596 --> 00:40:22,353
Did you two split up?

490
00:40:22,353 --> 00:40:24,905
She is pretty intense to work with. Right?

491
00:40:24,905 --> 00:40:28,429
She is filming in Canada.

492
00:40:28,429 --> 00:40:30,091
Canada?

493
00:40:30,786 --> 00:40:34,889
She owes me big time.

494
00:40:34,889 --> 00:40:37,357
- Sorry?
- Just a moment...

495
00:40:38,627 --> 00:40:39,952
But Director Woo,

496
00:40:39,952 --> 00:40:43,172
your style has gotten a lot more relaxed.

497
00:40:43,172 --> 00:40:45,457
Now you finally look like a director.

498
00:40:45,457 --> 00:40:47,085
Are you shooting anything these days?

499
00:40:47,085 --> 00:40:48,767
- Sir.
- Yes?

500
00:40:48,767 --> 00:40:51,841
Are we filming or not?

501
00:40:51,841 --> 00:40:53,398
Let's get started.

502
00:40:53,398 --> 00:40:55,075
I was just about to.

503
00:40:55,075 --> 00:40:57,842
Could you just take off that hoodie?

504
00:40:57,842 --> 00:40:59,032
I'll take it off.

505
00:40:59,032 --> 00:41:01,439
Yes, please.

506
00:41:09,867 --> 00:41:12,152
Oh my gosh... It's been ages.

507
00:41:12,152 --> 00:41:14,904
How have you been?

508
00:41:14,904 --> 00:41:16,332
I missed you so much.

509
00:41:16,332 --> 00:41:19,078
Wow. You look so pretty.

510
00:42:02,126 --> 00:42:04,059
Hey.

511
00:42:04,059 --> 00:42:05,991
I thought you were in Canada.

512
00:42:05,991 --> 00:42:07,516
You look great.

513
00:42:07,516 --> 00:42:08,800
What are you doing here?

514
00:42:08,800 --> 00:42:11,102
I'm just here for...

515
00:42:20,825 --> 00:42:22,210
Hey.

516
00:42:22,795 --> 00:42:24,696
I can't breathe.

517
00:42:27,402 --> 00:42:30,120
Oh, right. I was making coffee.

518
00:42:30,120 --> 00:42:32,863
- Right! The coffee!
- Camera! Camera!

519
00:42:32,863 --> 00:42:35,066
I really want to film this.

520
00:42:35,066 --> 00:42:36,291
Come get your coffee.

521
00:42:36,291 --> 00:42:38,286
I made it cold enough to freeze you solid.

522
00:42:38,286 --> 00:42:39,657
Decaf, right?

523
00:42:39,657 --> 00:42:41,083
Where are you?

524
00:42:41,083 --> 00:42:43,036
That bistro again?

525
00:42:43,036 --> 00:42:45,724
You're reading?

526
00:42:49,789 --> 00:42:51,548
You're real.

527
00:42:52,714 --> 00:42:54,836
You're really Ju Yi Jae.

528
00:42:54,836 --> 00:42:56,731
Have you been well?

529
00:43:05,842 --> 00:43:07,046
What is this?

530
00:43:07,046 --> 00:43:09,650
Curtains shut in the middle of the day?

531
00:43:10,413 --> 00:43:12,072
What a mess.

532
00:43:12,072 --> 00:43:14,507
You used to be so neat.

533
00:43:15,259 --> 00:43:17,076
When did you get here?

534
00:43:17,076 --> 00:43:18,872
Early this morning.

535
00:43:20,459 --> 00:43:22,003
Why?

536
00:43:22,003 --> 00:43:24,105
Guess why.

537
00:43:25,319 --> 00:43:27,950
The Geumseong Film Festival opens in two weeks.

538
00:43:27,950 --> 00:43:31,180
I'm nominated for the Rising Director Award.

539
00:43:31,841 --> 00:43:33,332
I see.

540
00:43:34,601 --> 00:43:37,356
What? No congratulations?

541
00:43:37,356 --> 00:43:40,557
After the festival... are you going back?

542
00:43:40,557 --> 00:43:41,962
I don't know.

543
00:43:41,962 --> 00:43:43,918
That depends on you.

544
00:43:46,773 --> 00:43:50,644
Then what do I have to do?

545
00:43:50,644 --> 00:43:52,637
Do you have a girlfriend?

546
00:43:54,717 --> 00:43:56,577
Guess not.

547
00:43:57,740 --> 00:44:00,443
- Want to make a movie with me?
- What?

548
00:44:05,957 --> 00:44:08,084
[Dream, Written by Woo Soo Bin]

549
00:44:08,084 --> 00:44:12,348
I found out in Canada
that you wrote my recommendation.

550
00:44:13,009 --> 00:44:17,795
I think I've grown enough
to stand proudly beside you now.

551
00:44:17,795 --> 00:44:20,428
Make a movie with me, Woo Soo Bin.

552
00:44:22,249 --> 00:44:23,879
Can I kiss you?

553
00:44:23,879 --> 00:44:26,122
- Are you going to?
- Yes.

554
00:44:26,729 --> 00:44:28,100
No.

555
00:44:28,100 --> 00:44:30,399
I meant the movie.

556
00:44:35,765 --> 00:44:37,192
Yes.

557
00:44:43,998 --> 00:44:45,775
Directors?

558
00:44:46,418 --> 00:44:47,561
Excuse me.

559
00:44:47,561 --> 00:44:49,259
Why aren't you coming out?

560
00:44:49,259 --> 00:44:52,480
Can we clock out now?

561
00:44:54,571 --> 00:44:57,425
What are they doing?

562
00:44:57,425 --> 00:44:59,638
Directors.

563
00:44:59,638 --> 00:45:01,701
Could you open the door?

564
00:45:07,854 --> 00:45:13,394
The Rising Director Award
at the 16th Geumseong Film Festival goes to...

565
00:45:15,639 --> 00:45:17,769
Director Ju Yi Jae of "Love Like A Dream."

566
00:45:17,769 --> 00:45:19,449
Congratulations.

567
00:45:19,449 --> 00:45:22,244
Director Ju Yi Jae completed
"Love Like A Dream"

568
00:45:22,244 --> 00:45:25,494
through the International
Cinema Residency Program.

569
00:45:25,494 --> 00:45:28,128
The film was praised for
bringing to life a fantastical world

570
00:45:28,128 --> 00:45:32,775
between dreams and reality
with her own convincing vision.

571
00:45:38,722 --> 00:45:40,894
Congratulations, Yi Jae.

572
00:45:44,156 --> 00:45:46,542
I won an award!

573
00:45:50,522 --> 00:45:52,541
Thank you.

574
00:45:54,466 --> 00:45:58,610
"Love Like A Dream"
was a bold challenge for me.

575
00:45:58,610 --> 00:46:00,789
My first solo film.

576
00:46:00,789 --> 00:46:03,623
Writing a script in an unfamiliar place.

577
00:46:03,623 --> 00:46:06,836
Working with an international crew...

578
00:46:06,836 --> 00:46:09,679
It was so hard.

579
00:46:10,372 --> 00:46:13,629
But I held on for one reason.

580
00:46:14,296 --> 00:46:20,578
I wanted to become someone worthy
of standing beside the person I love.

581
00:46:21,967 --> 00:46:24,930
I loved my dream with all my heart.

582
00:46:24,930 --> 00:46:27,667
<i>Yes. Let's make it together.</i>

583
00:46:27,667 --> 00:46:28,967
<i>Come here!</i>

584
00:46:28,967 --> 00:46:30,772
<i>- Come here.
- Stop!</i>

585
00:46:30,772 --> 00:46:32,103
<i>Let me go!</i>

586
00:46:32,103 --> 00:46:35,567
The more I loved it, the more I hated it.

587
00:46:35,567 --> 00:46:37,525
<i>You bastard.</i>

588
00:46:39,780 --> 00:46:43,603
I tried to forget it,
but in the end, I came back.

589
00:46:43,603 --> 00:46:45,720
<i>Excuse me.</i>

590
00:46:52,820 --> 00:46:55,999
Right now, it feels like...

591
00:46:55,999 --> 00:47:00,978
I went through a love like war
and somehow reached a dramatic truce.

592
00:47:01,924 --> 00:47:07,367
Someday, we may go at each other
like enemies again.

593
00:47:07,367 --> 00:47:09,824
But I'm not worried.

594
00:47:09,824 --> 00:47:14,782
Because I've become a bigger person.

595
00:47:16,098 --> 00:47:21,780
So I'll keep fighting this love like war.

596
00:47:21,780 --> 00:47:23,673
Thank you!

597
00:48:28,679 --> 00:48:30,129
<i>Ready...</i>

598
00:48:30,129 --> 00:48:31,964
<i>Action!</i>

599
00:48:36,538 --> 00:48:39,095
<i>Enough with the filming.</i>

600
00:48:39,095 --> 00:48:41,251
<i>Come taste this.</i>

601
00:48:43,684 --> 00:48:45,540
<i>Good! It's just right.</i>

602
00:48:45,540 --> 00:48:47,885
<i>- Is it too bland?</i>
- No.

603
00:48:48,869 --> 00:48:50,409
Perfect.

604
00:48:52,703 --> 00:48:54,793
- Mom.
- Yes?

605
00:48:54,793 --> 00:48:58,213
Is there anything you want to do?

606
00:48:58,213 --> 00:48:59,643
Why all of a sudden?

607
00:48:59,643 --> 00:49:04,420
I heard Soo Bin's mom
and the guesthouse grandma travel together.

608
00:49:04,420 --> 00:49:07,225
Want to go on a weeklong trip with me?

609
00:49:07,225 --> 00:49:08,619
Forget it.

610
00:49:08,619 --> 00:49:11,316
I can't just leave my customers.

611
00:49:11,316 --> 00:49:14,076
Then let's close the shop.

612
00:49:14,076 --> 00:49:16,773
Young Jae makes money now too.

613
00:49:16,773 --> 00:49:18,447
Yi Jae.

614
00:49:20,666 --> 00:49:23,363
I was too busy scraping by.

615
00:49:23,363 --> 00:49:26,739
The shop never made me happy.

616
00:49:26,739 --> 00:49:30,329
Every morning, opening the shop felt so heavy.

617
00:49:30,946 --> 00:49:33,884
But these days, the door feels lighter.

618
00:49:35,233 --> 00:49:38,558
I guess I'm finally at ease

619
00:49:38,558 --> 00:49:41,447
now that you and Young Jae
have found your own way.

620
00:49:42,628 --> 00:49:46,421
For now, I want to run the shop in peace.

621
00:49:48,602 --> 00:49:52,560
<i>When I get tired of it, I'll quit. Okay?</i>

622
00:49:55,338 --> 00:49:58,588
Once you quit, you have to travel with me.

623
00:49:58,588 --> 00:50:00,339
Okay.

624
00:50:00,339 --> 00:50:01,972
Promise.

625
00:50:03,175 --> 00:50:05,169
<i>Like this?</i>

626
00:50:10,093 --> 00:50:12,531
Then I'm off.

627
00:50:12,531 --> 00:50:14,082
Where are you going?

628
00:50:14,082 --> 00:50:15,575
To see Soo Bin.

629
00:50:15,575 --> 00:50:18,081
- Hey, Yi Jae.
- Yeah?

630
00:50:18,081 --> 00:50:20,987
All that talking, and you forgot to sign?

631
00:50:20,987 --> 00:50:23,219
Oh, right.

632
00:50:24,949 --> 00:50:26,649
Wait.

633
00:50:26,649 --> 00:50:29,228
- Here it is.
- Oh my.

634
00:50:33,093 --> 00:50:36,589
But do these people even know who I am?

635
00:50:36,589 --> 00:50:37,643
Of course.

636
00:50:37,643 --> 00:50:39,989
Film director Ju Yi Jae.

637
00:50:40,816 --> 00:50:43,728
I doubt they've all seen my movies.

638
00:50:43,728 --> 00:50:46,068
Yeah, they haven't.

639
00:50:46,068 --> 00:50:47,486
What?

640
00:50:47,486 --> 00:50:51,487
So I told them, "No movie, no autograph."

641
00:50:51,487 --> 00:50:53,372
I knew it.

642
00:50:54,346 --> 00:50:56,637
- Alright...
- Get to it.

643
00:50:56,637 --> 00:50:59,414
"'Gyeongseong Love Song'

644
00:50:59,414 --> 00:51:00,967
Director.

645
00:51:00,967 --> 00:51:03,007
Ju Yi Jae."

646
00:51:03,007 --> 00:51:04,672
How's that?

647
00:51:04,672 --> 00:51:07,678
- Great!
- Right?

648
00:51:08,972 --> 00:51:11,442
Are your mom and Grandma coming today?

649
00:51:11,442 --> 00:51:14,188
They should be arriving right about now.

650
00:51:20,179 --> 00:51:22,216
Guys! We're here!

651
00:51:22,216 --> 00:51:23,569
Grandma!

652
00:51:23,569 --> 00:51:24,603
Soo Bin.

653
00:51:24,603 --> 00:51:26,593
Yi Jae, get in.

654
00:51:26,593 --> 00:51:28,037
Get in.

655
00:51:33,944 --> 00:51:36,397
Let's go!

656
00:51:36,397 --> 00:51:40,467
- I brought something.
- She worked hard to find it.

657
00:51:40,467 --> 00:51:42,207
[Sea Trip: Saw the ocean with Hwa Yeon today]
Wow.

658
00:51:42,207 --> 00:51:44,647
All the way to Gangneung?

659
00:51:45,290 --> 00:51:47,924
I thought all oceans were the same.

660
00:51:47,924 --> 00:51:51,010
But the one there was different from ours.

661
00:51:51,010 --> 00:51:55,373
The waves here are calm, like me.
Like they've lived a whole life.

662
00:51:55,373 --> 00:51:59,178
But Gangneung's waves were so blue and strong,

663
00:51:59,178 --> 00:52:01,226
just like you kids.

664
00:52:01,226 --> 00:52:04,896
To me, you looked just like
the waves in Gangneung.

665
00:52:04,896 --> 00:52:06,481
Yeah?

666
00:52:06,481 --> 00:52:11,608
She kept grumbling until we left,
saying, "Why go anywhere at my age?"

667
00:52:11,608 --> 00:52:13,697
But once we got there...

668
00:52:14,442 --> 00:52:17,576
She had more energy than I did.

669
00:52:17,576 --> 00:52:20,005
I can't travel with Hwa Yeon anymore.

670
00:52:20,005 --> 00:52:22,658
We walk 30 minutes, and she says, "Let's rest."

671
00:52:22,658 --> 00:52:24,748
Then, "Let's get coffee."

672
00:52:24,748 --> 00:52:26,772
We barely looked around.

673
00:52:26,772 --> 00:52:30,714
We didn't go there
just to sit and drink coffee.

674
00:52:30,714 --> 00:52:32,174
Am I wrong?

675
00:52:32,174 --> 00:52:35,186
You're right. Grandma is right.

676
00:52:35,186 --> 00:52:39,513
Then where do you want to go next, Grandma?

677
00:52:39,513 --> 00:52:43,143
<i>I could even go to the States now.</i>

678
00:52:43,143 --> 00:52:46,689
<i>I want to fly on a plane before I die.</i>

679
00:52:46,689 --> 00:52:48,427
Let's go together.

680
00:52:48,427 --> 00:52:51,891
No! Not with you!

681
00:52:51,891 --> 00:52:54,288
Come on. You'd miss me.

682
00:52:54,288 --> 00:52:55,656
Miss you? Please.

683
00:52:55,656 --> 00:52:58,864
- Come with me.
- Then just go with me.

684
00:52:58,864 --> 00:53:01,406
- Should I?
- Yi Jae, you come too.

685
00:53:01,406 --> 00:53:04,498
So the main character finally escapes!

686
00:53:04,498 --> 00:53:05,914
But then, the twist!

687
00:53:05,914 --> 00:53:08,870
Right in front of him,
the ending credits start rolling!

688
00:53:08,870 --> 00:53:10,042
With the game company logo.

689
00:53:10,042 --> 00:53:11,746
Chills!

690
00:53:11,746 --> 00:53:13,423
He was inside the game all along.

691
00:53:13,423 --> 00:53:14,455
What do you think?

692
00:53:14,455 --> 00:53:16,979
Can you feel it? Yeah?

693
00:53:18,175 --> 00:53:20,632
If this becomes a movie, it'll be huge.

694
00:53:20,632 --> 00:53:23,016
- The braised radish is good today, right?
- Try this too.

695
00:53:23,016 --> 00:53:25,769
Come on, listen! This is my dream!

696
00:53:25,769 --> 00:53:27,479
My novel becoming a movie!

697
00:53:27,479 --> 00:53:29,525
Kim Jin Su.

698
00:53:31,075 --> 00:53:33,098
Yi Jae!

699
00:53:35,466 --> 00:53:36,488
You useless man.

700
00:53:36,488 --> 00:53:39,909
- Seong Chan.
- I told you to pick up Seong Chan today.

701
00:53:39,909 --> 00:53:41,786
- Oh, right...
- "Oh, right?"

702
00:53:41,786 --> 00:53:43,756
"Dream," my foot.

703
00:53:43,756 --> 00:53:46,796
My dream is for you to become human.

704
00:53:46,796 --> 00:53:47,833
Get over here.

705
00:53:47,833 --> 00:53:49,633
I'll make you human.

706
00:53:49,633 --> 00:53:52,042
- Okay! Stay back!
- Come here!

707
00:53:53,080 --> 00:53:54,197
What is that?

708
00:53:54,197 --> 00:53:56,804
This? A camera.

709
00:53:56,804 --> 00:53:58,317
Want to see?

710
00:53:59,004 --> 00:54:02,271
That seems a little violent for a kid to watch.

711
00:54:02,271 --> 00:54:03,468
It's okay.

712
00:54:03,468 --> 00:54:06,306
I'm in elementary school now.

713
00:54:06,306 --> 00:54:07,368
Seong Chan.

714
00:54:07,368 --> 00:54:09,392
What do you want to be when you grow up?

715
00:54:09,392 --> 00:54:13,423
Mom said I should become anything but Dad.

716
00:54:14,593 --> 00:54:16,346
Their spicy fish stew is amazing.

717
00:54:16,346 --> 00:54:18,780
Let's come back. This place is my new favorite.

718
00:54:18,780 --> 00:54:20,482
I'm full.

719
00:54:21,356 --> 00:54:24,336
[SimSim Fisheries]
Looks like he's doing well.

720
00:54:25,978 --> 00:54:27,082
<i>Hey.</i>

721
00:54:27,082 --> 00:54:29,249
<i>You stay seated.</i>

722
00:54:29,249 --> 00:54:31,313
I'm proud of him.

723
00:54:31,313 --> 00:54:33,832
Why are you proud of my brother?

724
00:54:33,832 --> 00:54:36,110
He's my brother-in-law.

725
00:54:36,110 --> 00:54:37,202
What?

726
00:54:37,839 --> 00:54:39,555
I should help him out.

727
00:54:39,555 --> 00:54:41,022
Brother-in-law, wait.

728
00:54:41,022 --> 00:54:42,426
Please stay seated.

729
00:54:42,426 --> 00:54:44,679
- No, I'll help.
- No, it's okay.

730
00:54:44,679 --> 00:54:46,243
Please...

731
00:54:46,243 --> 00:54:47,596
My brother-in-law.

732
00:54:47,596 --> 00:54:49,540
Gosh... "Brother-in-law?"

733
00:54:49,540 --> 00:54:52,033
Unbelievable.

734
00:54:56,026 --> 00:54:57,406
<i>Brother-in-law.</i>

735
00:54:58,323 --> 00:55:00,053
<i>I love you.</i>

736
00:55:00,053 --> 00:55:01,346
<i>Love you too.</i>

737
00:55:04,213 --> 00:55:06,749
I'm curious about something.

738
00:55:06,749 --> 00:55:08,039
What?

739
00:55:08,039 --> 00:55:09,952
Didn't you miss me?

740
00:55:09,952 --> 00:55:11,689
What kind of question is that?

741
00:55:11,689 --> 00:55:13,737
Then how could you not call me once?

742
00:55:13,737 --> 00:55:15,142
You're so cold.

743
00:55:15,142 --> 00:55:16,483
I did.

744
00:55:16,483 --> 00:55:17,921
Sorry?

745
00:55:17,921 --> 00:55:18,924
Nothing.

746
00:55:18,924 --> 00:55:23,337
Then did you lose sleep,
skip meals, drink, and cry?

747
00:55:23,337 --> 00:55:25,263
Who do you think I am?

748
00:55:25,263 --> 00:55:28,172
It wasn't that bad.

749
00:55:30,466 --> 00:55:32,517
<i>"Ju Yi Jae..."</i>

750
00:55:32,517 --> 00:55:35,863
<i>Damn it. Here he goes again.</i>

751
00:55:35,863 --> 00:55:38,065
<i>Don't disappear!</i>

752
00:55:38,065 --> 00:55:39,127
<i>No!</i>

753
00:55:39,127 --> 00:55:41,887
<i>Telepathy. Telepathy.</i>

754
00:55:41,887 --> 00:55:43,837
<i>Ju Yi Jae.</i>

755
00:55:43,837 --> 00:55:47,200
<i>Come here right now.</i>

756
00:55:47,200 --> 00:55:49,224
<i>Right now.</i>

757
00:55:49,224 --> 00:55:51,877
<i>Mom, that man is weird.</i>

758
00:55:51,877 --> 00:55:53,454
<i>Don't stare.</i>

759
00:55:53,454 --> 00:55:55,028
<i>Come here right now!</i>

760
00:55:55,028 --> 00:55:56,899
<i>Oh my gosh...</i>

761
00:55:56,899 --> 00:55:59,423
<i>I used to make hangover soup for my daughter.</i>

762
00:55:59,423 --> 00:56:02,441
<i>Now I have to make yours too?</i>

763
00:56:02,441 --> 00:56:03,427
<i>Hello.</i>

764
00:56:03,427 --> 00:56:06,150
<i>Yi Jae, don't go...</i>

765
00:56:18,026 --> 00:56:19,719
I was...

766
00:56:20,786 --> 00:56:22,865
perfectly calm while I waited.

767
00:56:22,865 --> 00:56:25,068
But you did wait.

768
00:56:26,168 --> 00:56:28,948
Of course.

769
00:56:28,948 --> 00:56:30,725
You were coming back.

770
00:56:30,725 --> 00:56:32,565
I could've settled down in Canada.

771
00:56:32,565 --> 00:56:34,705
I'd report you for overstaying.

772
00:56:34,705 --> 00:56:36,877
I could've stayed there legally.

773
00:56:36,877 --> 00:56:39,215
Then I would've gone there.

774
00:56:39,215 --> 00:56:41,942
I might not have welcomed you.

775
00:56:41,942 --> 00:56:44,706
Why wouldn't you?

776
00:56:44,706 --> 00:56:47,462
Maybe I got a new boyfriend.

777
00:56:47,462 --> 00:56:49,355
A handsome boyfriend.

778
00:56:49,355 --> 00:56:51,838
A sexy boyfriend.

779
00:56:52,888 --> 00:56:54,491
More than me?

780
00:56:57,939 --> 00:56:59,083
Get home safe.

781
00:56:59,083 --> 00:57:01,396
Sexy, handsome Soo Bin.

782
00:57:04,936 --> 00:57:06,545
Yi Jae.

783
00:57:11,340 --> 00:57:12,900
Will you...

784
00:57:13,664 --> 00:57:15,748
stay with me tonight?

785
00:57:41,422 --> 00:57:43,033
Hurry!

786
00:58:22,720 --> 00:58:24,325
That tickles.

787
00:58:24,325 --> 00:58:26,038
Deal with it.

788
00:58:33,266 --> 00:58:35,969
I lost this.

789
00:58:35,969 --> 00:58:39,179
Tie your hair, then keep going.

790
00:58:39,179 --> 00:58:40,656
Wait.

791
00:58:40,656 --> 00:58:42,885
Were you at the airport that day?

792
00:58:47,821 --> 00:58:49,167
Yes.

793
00:58:50,029 --> 00:58:51,865
And...

794
00:58:53,482 --> 00:58:55,117
this.

795
00:59:05,094 --> 00:59:06,771
What is this?

796
00:59:11,764 --> 00:59:13,573
My dream.

797
00:59:16,816 --> 00:59:18,148
Cut!

798
00:59:18,743 --> 00:59:20,038
"Cut?"

799
00:59:40,093 --> 00:59:41,449
Okay!

800
00:59:41,449 --> 00:59:43,007
Okay!

801
00:59:54,734 --> 00:59:58,099
[Dream to You]

802
01:00:08,921 --> 01:00:11,747
[Thank you for watching "Dream to You"]

